# Custom design rules -- rtk-gps-module.
#
# KiCad auto-loads this file because its name matches the project name.
# Board-wide minimums live in the project file (Board Setup > Design Rules
# > Constraints); this file only carves out the one case where a board-wide
# rule is wrong by construction.
#
# Syntax follows the working files in stm32mp157-devkit and red-light-panel.

(version 1)

# A castellated pad is a plated half-hole: the board outline router runs
# straight through the middle of the drill, so the pad MUST reach the edge.
# The board-wide 0.5 mm copper-to-edge rule is correct for every other
# object on this board and wrong for these 24 pads, which it flags as 24
# errors that can never be cleared.
#
# Without this carve-out DRC is unusable as a gate: 24 permanent errors
# bury whatever real error appears next during routing.
#
# Scoped by courtyard rather than by net, because the castellated pads
# carry ordinary nets (GND, 5V_IN, TXD1 ...) that must keep full edge
# clearance everywhere else on the board.
# No positive minimum can satisfy this: the pad does not merely touch the
# outline, it crosses it, so the measured clearance is negative and
# (min 0mm) still fails. The constraint has to be switched off for these
# pads rather than relaxed.
(rule "castellated pads reach the board edge by design"
	(severity ignore)
	(constraint edge_clearance)
	(condition "A.insideCourtyard('J501') || A.insideCourtyard('J502')")
)
